FAQ = [
 ("How much can a 2020–2025 Palisade tow?",
  "Hyundai's 2023 Palisade spec sheet lists 5,000 lb with trailer brakes and 1,650 lb without, for both FWD and AWD. The unbraked figure is the one people miss: a small utility trailer loaded with a mower or firewood can pass 1,650 lb, and above that Hyundai expects the trailer to have its own brakes. Weigh a loaded utility trailer once; many owners are surprised by the number."),
 ("Does the Palisade come ready to tow?",
  "Partly. Hyundai's 2023 spec sheet lists pre-wiring and a heavy-duty transmission oil cooler as standard trailering equipment. What it doesn't list is a hitch. So on most Palisades, the cooling is already there and the wiring is prepared, and you add a receiver and a harness that plugs into the factory connector. We confirmed this for 2023; check the sticker on earlier trucks."),
 ("Is the Palisade hitch the same as the Kia Telluride's?",
  "Sometimes. Draw-Tite's 76420 is listed for both, as are most budget Amazon hitches and Stealth Hitches' 2020–2022 conversion kit. CURT, though, sells separate parts: 13427 for the Palisade (39 lb) and 13420 for the Telluride (33 lb). Buy a listing that names the Palisade. If a listing names only the Telluride, ask the seller before assuming it fits; CURT's two parts differ in weight and design."),
 ("What changed for the 2023 facelift?",
  "For hitch buyers, mainly wiring and hidden-hitch parts. CURT's 56420 4-way harness lists the 2020–2022 Palisade only, and Stealth Hitches sells separate towing conversion kits for 2020–2022 (SHT25031, $299) and 2023–2025 (SHT25031A, $399). The CURT and Draw-Tite hitches cover 2020–2025 with one part, so a hitch bought for a 2021 still fits if you trade up to a 2024."),
 ("What is a Stealth hitch and can it tow?",
  "Stealth Hitches makes a receiver that stays hidden when not in use. The Amazon listing here is the rack package, meant for bike racks and carriers. To tow with it, Stealth sells a conversion kit with safety chain anchors, a harness and controller kit, 7-way brackets, a 7-way to 4-way adapter, a ball mount and a 2 in ball. The pages we read didn't give a tow rating, so ask Stealth before towing."),
 ("Does self-leveling suspension change the tow rating?",
  "No. Hyundai lists self-leveling rear suspension on SEL Premium and up in its 2023 spec sheet, and the tow rating is the same 5,000 lb on every trim. Self-leveling keeps the rear from squatting under tongue load. On an SE or SEL without it, a weight-distribution setup does a similar job, and Draw-Tite's 76420 is rated for one."),
 ("Which hitch has the highest rating?",
  "With weight distribution, the Draw-Tite 76420 at 6,000 lb GTW and 750 lb tongue weight; CURT rates the 13427 the same with WD. Without WD, both are rated 5,000 lb GTW, with 750 lb tongue weight for the CURT and 500 lb for the Draw-Tite. The Palisade's own 5,000 lb limit applies either way; a higher hitch rating doesn't raise it."),
 ("Do I need a brake controller?",
  "If your trailer has electric brakes, yes, and Hyundai's 1,650 lb unbraked limit means most trailers over that weight should. CURT's 51529 quick-plug harness lets a CURT brake controller plug into the factory socket on 2021–2025 Palisades, per CURT. For 2020 models, ask the seller. A 7-way connector is also needed, and Stealth's conversion kits include 7-way brackets."),
 ("Will these hitches fit the 2026 Palisade?",
  "No. The 2026 Palisade is a new generation with a new body. Every product on this page is listed for 2020–2025, the first generation only. For a 2026, buy only from a listing that names it. That includes harnesses, which are the most year-specific part of the setup, and hidden-hitch kits like Stealth's."),
 ("Is the Reese hitch-and-wiring bundle worth it?",
  "It's convenient for a 2023–2025 Palisade, because the wiring is where the facelift changed things. The listing pairs a Reese hitch with a 4-way harness for 2023–2025 models. It doesn't name the Reese part number in its title, so ask the seller which hitch and harness are in the box and what the hitch is rated for."),
]

